<newsitem itemid="422621" id="root" date="1997-03-05" xml:lang="en">
<title>NORWAY: Storebrand 1996 group profits fall.</title>
<headline>Storebrand 1996 group profits fall.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31</p>
<p>				     (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating result		     4,120	   vs	  4,206</p>
<p> Group result			   1,254	   vs	  1,451</p>
<p> EPS    (crowns)			 4.10	   vs	   4.94</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Norway's biggest insurance company is Storebrand ASA. Eight analysts polled by Reuters had expected the company to post 1996 group profits of 1.16 billion crowns.  </p>
<p> Life assurance			 3,427	   vs	  3,337</p>
<p> Life, Storebrand share		 561	   vs	    582</p>
<p> Non-life insurance		   1,043	   vs	  1,184</p>
<p> Life policyholder portion	  2,866	   vs	  2,755</p>
<p>NOTE - The board proposed a dividend of 0.70 crowns per preferential share, unchanged from 1995.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
